{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeufbgMLDFoKYyYhQjeGz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I did **not** delete or skip the failing test — that would have masked a real defect and violated this repo's explicit \"no unrelated failures, stop and ask\" and \"done means green\" rules in AGENTS.md. Instead I found and fixed the actual bug:\n\n**Root cause**: `ShouldRaise.__exit__` (`src/testfixtures/shouldraise.py`) had a pre-check `type(self.exception) is not type(actual)` meant to short-circuit before calling `compare()`. That's correct when `self.exception` is a plain exception instance, but `repr_like`/`str_like` (documented, tested public API) pass a `ReprComparison`/`StrComparison` object instead — whose own type is never the raised exception's type, so the check always failed and legitimate matches were rejected.\n\n**Fix**: when `self.exception` is a `RenderingComparison`, compare against its `.type` attribute (the type it actually expects) instead of `type(self.exception)`.\n\nResult: `python -m pytest` now passes fully — 1215 passed, 31 skipped, 0 failed.\n\nOne caveat: `uv` and `mypy` aren't available in this sandbox, so I couldn't run the full `./happy.sh` gate (it fails immediately on `uv: command not found`, unrelated to this change). Pytest itself is fully green. Let me know if you'd like me to try installing `uv`/`mypy` here, or if you'll run `happy.sh` in your normal environment before merging."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":718,"cache_read_input_tokens":58983,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":718},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"51c8f01a-2dc3-46b3-b225-466b8e51b200","uuid":"b148fef0-970f-46f8-83af-d06e28136cb5